3 Usage
*******

Here are the primary interactive commands and functions provided by
‘cpf-tools’:

‘cpf-tools-generate-cpf (&optional arg)’
     Generate a valid CPF number.  Prefix arguments control output and
     insertion:
        • ‘nil’: Output unformatted to ‘*Messages*’.
        • ‘C-u’: Insert unformatted at point.
        • ‘C-u C-u’: Output formatted to ‘*Messages*’.
        • ‘C-u C-u C-u’: Insert formatted at point.

‘cpf-tools-generate-cnpj (&optional arg)’
     Generate a valid CNPJ number (supports the same prefix arguments as
     ‘generate-cpf’).

‘cpf-tools-complete-cpf (incomplete-cpf-string)’
     Find and display valid CPF numbers matching an incomplete pattern
     with wildcards (‘*’ or ‘?’), such as ‘***.781.235-**’.

‘cpf-tools-complete-cnpj (incomplete-cnpj-string)’
     Find and display valid CNPJ numbers matching an incomplete pattern
     with wildcards (‘*’ or ‘?’).

‘cpf-tools-format-cpf-region (beg end)’
     Format the marked region as CPF.

‘cpf-tools-format-cnpj-region (beg end)’
     Format the marked region as CNPJ.

‘cpf-tools-format-cpf-cnpj-region (beg end)’
     Format the marked region as CPF or CNPJ automatically based on its
     length.



